# Code Quality Gates

After ANY code change, before reporting the task done:

1. Lint passes with zero errors and zero warnings (typically `yarn lint`).
2. Formatting is clean per the repo's Prettier config (typically `yarn format`).
3. Typecheck passes with zero errors (typically `yarn typecheck`; Svelte projects: `yarn check` for svelte-check + TS).

## Rules

- Fix lint/format/type issues you introduced — never leave them for later.
- Never weaken or edit lint/formatter configs to make a check pass; fix the code instead.
- No inline suppressions (`eslint-disable`, `ts-ignore`, ...) without a one-line justification comment on the same line.
- Prettier config stays as configured in the repo — do not override it with local options or inline pragmas.
- If the project lacks one of these scripts, say so explicitly instead of silently skipping the gate.
